==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Afterschool Sakura''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Sacred Blade Sakura''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Sacred Blade Sakura Z''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Sakura Sonic's high damage makes her [[Critical Hit]]s lethal to any Metal, but her low Crit chance makes it unreliable. She is intended to be the ultimate [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal]] debuffer, with three anti-Metal abilities: [[Slow|Slow]]ing Metals down, [[Weaken|Weaken]]ing them to 50% at a 100% chance, and only taking 1/4~1/5 damage from them through [[Resistant|Resist]]. This allows her to easily crowd-control Metal enemies to buy time for other [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] to finish them off. Sakura also has fantastic synergy with long-ranged Critters, such as [[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]], [[Marauder Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Paladin Cat]] and [[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Kubilan Pasalan]], as she can prevent them from getting close for quite a while. However, [[Super Metal Hippoe]] is still troublesome as she isn't immune to his knockback, so other sources of support are still necessary.

==='''True Form'''===
Sacred Blade Sakura may look like an underwhelming True Form, only improving her resistance to take 1/6~1/7 damage from Metals, but by putting her in the first row, she will activate a [[Cat Combo]] called [[Ninjutsu Cute (Combo)|Ninjutsu Cute]], one of the only Combos to increase Critical chance. While it's only a 1% additive chance by itself, it's a single-slot Combo, meaning it can be combined with the likes of [[Miracle Performance (Combo)|Miracle Performance]] and [[Whale Digger (Combo)|Whale Digger]]. Even that 1% chance can significantly increase the effectiveness of more spammable Critters like [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] and [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]], making the True Form worth it for that alone.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
Sacred Blade Sakura Z's first and arguably most important buff is an extra second to her Slow and Weaken effects, which gives enemy Metals even less time to deal damage. This is especially useful when she doesn't Crit, and improves her main niche substantially given her decently fast attack rate.

Also of great importance is her Omni Strike granting her 50 extra piercing range, allowing her to target peons and reach those enemies hiding just behind them. [[Metal Doge]] in particular goes from annoyance to stepping stone, as do mixed peons in Metal stages.

This Ultra Form also increases her Critical Hit chance from 5% to 8%, a solid increase in its own right while still being unreliable. However, on top of her existing Critical Combo, she gains another one exclusive to her Ultra Form called [[TopSecret (Combo)|#TopSecret]], increasing the effect by another 1%. This raises her own effective chance to 10% while also providing 2% to any other Critters in the lineup with a single slot.

Unfortunately, nothing can change the fact that she's still just an anti-Metal unit; it's generally not a good idea to spend such costly materials on a Metal specialist unit over powerful generalists. However, if one has excess [[Catseye|Dark Catseyes]] and Behemoth Gems to spare, they can do a whole lot worse than a phenomenal specialist Uber. Overall, not a bad investment, but there are still many Ultra Forms/Talents that would be a higher priority for 90% of players.

==='''Talents'''===
Sakura Sonic's Talents range from mediocre to situational. '''Defense Buff''' and '''Survives''' are probably the most worthwhile, since she can tank Metals better, and the Survive ability means she can continue to support your other anti-Metals for a fair amount of time, taking great advantage of her high range, though they are pretty expensive for what they do. '''Immune to [[Surge Attack|Surges]]''' rarely comes into play due to the rather uncommon combination of Metals and Surges which are better dealt with other units anyway, but '''Immune to [[Wave Attack|Waves]]''' can potentially see limited use against [[CyberFace]]/[[Koronium]], though again superior solutions exist to counter them already. '''Attack Buff''' is near-useless, as her low Critical chance means she usually has no hopes of eliminating Metals on her own, and there are plenty of better damage-dealers for non-Metal enemies.

