==Trivia==
*Sakura Sonic seems to be related to [[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]]. Both are [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal]] specialists with similarities in their attack animations, both hail from a ninja clan who opposes evil, the first lines of their Normal Forms' Japanese descriptions are nearly identical, their swords are both described as "swords of exorcism" (退魔の刀 ''taima no katana''), and the Japanese names of Oni Hayabusa and Sacred Blade Sakura both contain 天誅 ''tenchū'' ("Heaven's punishment" or "divine retribution"). Furthermore, the kanji 隼 in Sakura's Japanese surname (風隼, ''Kazehaya'') is pronounced ''hayabusa'' on its own.
*She is the second [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] to have an official animation shortly after her introduction, the first being [[Twinstars (Uber Rare Cat)|Twinstars]].
*''Sakura'' means "cherry blossom" in Japanese and is a very common name for Japanese girls.
*The "JK" in Afterschool Sakura's Japanese name, JK Sakura Kazehaya, is an acronym which stands for 女子高生 ''joshi kōsei'' (high school girl).
*The "Z" in Sacred Blade Sakura Z's name may stand for ''zenith'', 全力 ''zenryoku'' (all of one's power; whole energy), or 全方位 ''zenhōi'' ([[Omni Strike|omnidirectional]]).
*Sacred Blade Sakura Z's smartphone resembles an [[wikipedia:iPhone 11 Pro|iPhone 11 Pro]].
*The kanji that appears during Sakura Sonic's [[True Form|True]] and [[Ultra Form]] attack animations is most likely "桉", which is a Japanese conifer called Hinoki Cypress that is found in central Japan.
*Sakura Sonic has a [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] charm, Afterschool Sakura gains three more of Cat as well as [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] and [[CyberFace]], and Sacred Blade Sakura gains [[Snache]] and [[Gory]].

